The C++ keyword static has three meanings. It can be used with a class data member, a local variable, or a function name. When used with a static variable or function, it is a storage class, and when it is used with a data member, it is a data modifier. When a static data member or a local variable is declared, it has the storage duration static, as opposed to the automatic storage duration associated with normal local variables.

