static local variable

When a static local variable is used in a function, the static local variable is initialized only the first time the function is called, and subsequent function calls do not reinitialize the variable. Furthermore, when a static local variable is declared, it retains its value between function calls.

static data member

When used with a class data member, the data member is shared between all objects created from the class.

static member function

When a class member function is declared to be static, it is not associated with a specific object created from the class.

